    "meal_prep": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "m_sub": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Shuck it gently",
            "subheading_size": "subtitle-md",
            "secondary_color": true
          }
        },
        "m_head": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Release, then save the shells",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Thaw the bag in the fridge overnight. Slide a small, sharp knife under each scallop to release it from the shell, and trim off any tough connective tissue. Keep the prettiest shells: wash them, cover them with boiling water in a heatproof bowl to lift off anything left behind, then drain and let them cool completely before they go back on the plate.</p><p>Pat the scallops dry with paper towels before you dice them, then keep them covered in the fridge while you cut everything else.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_btn": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "Shop Half-Shell Scallops",
            "button_link": "/products/half-shell-scallops-2x-12oz-bag",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_size": "md",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "m_sub",
        "m_head",
        "m_text",
        "m_btn"
      ],
