    "faq": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q_thaw": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I thaw the scallops?",
            "text": "<p>Move the bag to the fridge the night before. Release them from the shells and pat them dry just before you dice them, and keep them cold until they go into the bowl.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_done": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is ceviche raw?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. The lime and passion fruit flavor the scallops and firm them a little, but they do not cook them, so ceviche is a raw dish. Eating raw or undercooked meat, poultry, seafood, shellfish or eggs may increase your risk of foodborne illness, especially with certain medical conditions. Consult your doctor if you think you may be sensitive.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_tear": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Which persimmons should I buy?",
            "text": "<p>Fuyu. They are the squat, tomato-shaped ones, and unlike Hachiya persimmons they are good to eat while still firm. Choose fruit that is ripe and sweet but holds its shape when finely diced.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_ahead": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can I make it ahead?",
            "text": "<p>Dice the persimmon, onion and pepper and wash the shells a few hours ahead, and keep everything in the fridge. Dice the scallops and dress the ceviche about 10 minutes before serving, and serve it immediately, while chilled.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_hold": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "It tastes too sweet. What do I do?",
            "text": "<p>Passion fruit and persimmons vary a lot in sweetness and acidity. Add more lime juice a little at a time, and another pinch of salt, until it tastes bright.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "q_sauce": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Can’t find passion fruit?",
            "text": "<p>Skip it. Miriam’s ceviche stands on its own with the lime and yuzu; you may want a little more lime.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "q_thaw",
        "q_done",
        "q_tear",
        "q_ahead",
        "q_hold",
        "q_sauce"
      ],
